{"finding_id":"F1","verdict":"refuted","refutation_attempt":"Confirmed that the sink is File.WriteAllText, which simply writes data to the filesystem; it does not execute a shell command. OS Command Injection requires constructing and executing a command string (e.g., via Process.Start or shell invocation). Path.Combine merely concatenates path components and does not spawn a process. Therefore, even with a malicious filePath, the code cannot lead to command execution.

Additionally, the code does not contain any system call or shell invocation that could be influenced by the filePath string.

Thus, the claim of OS Command Injection is invalid.","evidence_lines":[39,40],"confidence":0.95}
